    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To file a roof insurance claim in Utah, get an independent professional roof inspection first, take photos of the damage, and contact your insurance company's claims department with the exact date of the storm or loss. Request that your local contractor be present when the insurance adjuster inspects the property.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Pre-Claim Inspection and Documentation"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule an inspection: Hire a licensed local roofer to perform a detailed assessment before calling your insurer."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Gather evidence\n: Collect the contractor's written report, photo evidence of hail bruising or wind-torn shingles, and the specific date of the weather event."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Mitigate further loss: Place a temporary tarp over active leaks to stop interior damage, and save all receipts."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Filing the Claim"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Contact your insurer: Call your insurance company's claims center (avoiding speculative or casual language about wear-and-tear) to officially open the claim and secure a claim number."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review your policy: Confirm your deductible amount and whether your plan settles at Actual Cash Value (ACV) or Replacement Cost Value (RCV).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Note on representation: Opinions are mixed on Reddit regarding letting a roofing company file entirely on your behalf; many Utah homeowners prefer staying directly involved in communications to ensure total transparency."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Adjuster Assessment and Settlement"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the adjuster: Have your chosen contractor on-site during the insurance adjuster's inspection to point out functional damage and prevent missed items."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review the estimate: Compare the insurance payout scope line-by-line against your contractor's bid. File for supplemental funds if critical repairs or local building codes were left off the initial insurance estimate."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          9,
          10
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm or damage\noccurred (hail, heavy snow load, wind)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The name of your insurance provider"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more specific tips on handling their particular adjustment process."
      }
    ],
